        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 9: Python Programming for the Cloud\nP\u00e1ginas: 336-373\n\u2022 Technical requirements  (337)\n\u2022 Learning about the cloud options for Python applications  (337)\n  \u2022 Introducing Python development environments for the cloud  (337)\n  \u2022 Introducing cloud runtime options for Python  (340)\n\u2022 Building Python web services for cloud deployment  (342)\n  \u2022 Using Google Cloud SDK  (343)\n  \u2022 Using the GCP web console  (352)\n\u2022 Using Google Cloud Platform for data processing  (355)\n  \u2022 Learning the fundamentals of Apache Beam  (356)\n  \u2022 Introducing Apache Beam pipelines  (357)\n  \u2022 Building pipelines for Cloud Dataflow  (364)\n\u2022 Summary  (370)\n\u2022 Questions  (371)\n\u2022 Further reading  (371)\n\u2022 Answers  (371)\n9\nPython\nProgramming for\nthe Cloud\nCloud computing is a broad term that is used for a wide variety of use cases. These use\ncases include an offering of physical or virtual compute platforms, software development\nplatforms, big data processing platforms, storage, network functions, software services,\nand many more. In this chapter, we will explore Python for cloud computing from two\ncorrelated aspects. First, we will investigate the options of using Python for building\napplications for cloud runtimes. Then, we will extend our discussion of data-intensive\nprocessing, which we started in Chapter 8 , Scaling Out Python using Clusters , from clusters\nto cloud environments. The focus of the discussion in this chapter will largely center on\nthe three public cloud platforms; that is, Google Cloud Platform ( GCP ), Amazon Web\nServices ( AWS ), and Microsoft Azure .\nWe will cover the following topics in this chapter:\n\u2022I Learning about the cloud options for Python applications\n\u2022I Building Python web services for cloud deployment\n\u2022I Using Google Cloud Platform for data processing\n314     Python Programming for the Cloud\nBy the end of this chapter, you will know how to develop and deploy applications to\na cloud platform and how to use Apache Beam in general and for Google Cloud Platform.",
